{"id":"d61dce73a1dba932750729d5928832cef4b6ba028a33180536b445f44daa69ea","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:42.944472543Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nSub-issue of 215ee3.\n\n## What to build\n\nAfter a Sync, if operations, comments or set members arrived for a ticket that is deleted locally and are newer than its delete op, the user is told. Text output prints one stderr warning per ticket: `warning: N edit(s) landed on deleted ticket <short> (ti undelete <short> to restore)`. `ti sync --json` and `ti pull --json` carry a `warnings` array with entries `{kind: \"edit-on-deleted\", ticket, count}`. Exit status unaffected. JSON schema extended additively.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Two-clone CLI test: A deletes and syncs; B (not yet synced) comments and syncs; A syncs; A's stderr has the warning with the right count; stdout JSON has the `warnings` entry; exit 0\n- [ ] No warning when nothing landed on deleted tickets; `warnings` is an empty array in JSON\n- [ ] Schema updated and schema test green\n- [ ] Agent docs describe the warning"}}}